# Code owners for security-sensitive paths.
#
# Required review from a code owner is the mitigation for the PR disposition
# merge gate's listener-coverage-narrowing and required-check-provenance
# gaps (see docs/development/reviewing.md): a candidate PR can no longer
# merge a
# change under .github/workflows/ -- including narrowing
# pr-disposition-review-trigger.yml's pull_request_review.types coverage,
# or authoring an unrelated workflow that mints its own check run named
# "disposition" -- without an independent owner approving that exact
# change. This entry has no effect until a maintainer enables "Require
# review from Code Owners" on the branch protection ruleset for `main`
# (see docs/development/reviewing.md's PR disposition merge gate
# activation checklist) -- CODEOWNERS alone does not enforce anything.
#
# This file also owns itself (and the rest of .github/), per GitHub's own
# guidance that protecting a repository fully against unauthorized changes
# requires defining an owner for CODEOWNERS in addition to the paths it
# protects: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# Without this, a PR could narrow or remove the /.github/workflows/ rule
# below in one change, then narrow the listener's trigger coverage or spoof
# the disposition check name in a later, no-longer-covered change.
/.github/ @alaiba

/.github/workflows/ @alaiba
